Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_battmgr: retain reported Uke zero cycles

A successful firmware report of zero cycles is a representable counter, not
an absent reading. Do not group CYCLE_COUNT with positive-only capacity and
voltage fields. Keep negative/sentinel and oversized values unavailable.

Uke OEM 5712080a4b0c0b1a879e6d145c601c649ddaddfd, same-SoC Nord4 and shared
Peridot/upstream wrappers return the reported counter without rejecting zero.
Retain GPL-2.0-only Linux Foundation/Linaro/Qualcomm attribution. This change
does not qualify the firmware's counter semantics, health or pack lifetime.

--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
@@ -1871,6 +1871,8 @@
 		return value <= 10000 ? 0 : -ENODATA;
 	case BATT_SOH:
 		return value <= 100 ? 0 : -ENODATA;
+	case BATT_CYCLE_COUNT:
+		return value <= INT_MAX ? 0 : -ENODATA;
 	case BATT_TEMP:
 		return (s32)value == INT_MIN || (s32)value == INT_MAX ? -ENODATA : 0;
 	case BATT_VOLT_OCV:
@@ -1878,7 +1880,6 @@
 	case BATT_VOLT_MAX:
 	case BATT_CHG_FULL_DESIGN:
 	case BATT_CHG_FULL:
-	case BATT_CYCLE_COUNT:
 	case BATT_TTF_AVG:
 	case BATT_TTE_AVG:
 	case BATT_RESISTANCE:
